Name: replicaonly
Type: SWITCH
Default-Value: 0
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

If enabled, marks the server as only being a replica: its data comes from
replication, and local changes are refused as temporary failures.  IMAP
writes get ``NO [UNAVAILABLE]``, JMAP writes get ``serverUnavailable``,
DAV writes get a 503, and delivery gets a 4.2.1 tempfail.  calalarmd runs
in dry-run mode, and cyr_expire only cleans up messages that are already
expunged.

A single user can be treated the same way on any server with ``cyr_deny -r``.
See also ``auth_notreplicaonly``.
